5. Modifications made by this integration
-----------------------------------------
Code changes (all runtime/native sources stay otherwise verbatim):

  * Text-only build. The Vision encoder contexts, the image frontend and the
    image request path are removed from what is installed. Requests carrying
    image content are rejected by the runtime instead of being silently
    downgraded; there is no vision support in this package.
  * 2K only. Only the 2,048-token envelope (models/2k + contracts/2k) is
    installed. The 4K profile is not built, not shipped and not selectable.
  * Repackaged for Yocto/Debian. Upstream install.py (platform gate, package
    version lock, binary SHA-256 gate, board-side g++ build, cp 4-7 affinity
    check) is not used. The native engine is cross-compiled by the recipe, the
    runtime configuration (runtime.json) is generated at build time with fixed
    paths, and the Python dependency closure comes from unpacked PyPI wheels
    instead of a venv created on the board.
  * Relocated file layout. Upstream's single installation directory is split
    into /usr/lib/qwen35 (runtime, engine, launch and wrappers) and
    /usr/share/qwen35 (read-only model assets), with all paths resolved through
    runtime.json. Nothing is written into the application directory at runtime.
  * Service integration. A systemd unit starts the server at boot on
    127.0.0.1:8000 and stops it cleanly; scratch, metrics and logs live under
    /run and /var/log instead of the installation directory.

Asset changes: none. Every downloaded file is installed byte-identical and is
verified against the upstream SHA-256 before use.

6. Development disclosure
-------------------------
Portions of this integration (recipe text, relocation logic, documentation)
were written with AI assistance and reviewed against the upstream sources.
Performance and accuracy figures quoted in README.md are the upstream project's
own measurements on Radxa Dragon Q6A (same QCS6490 / HTP v68 SoC), not
measurements taken on the Quectel PI H1.
